      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ROCKTEX (1) trialled well coming into the campaign and flew home from the back over 1100m at Northam fresh. Out to 1300m is a big tick for this colt who may be able to sit a touch closer. He's an improving commodity who finds a very winnable event second-up. AURA MAGNA (5) will find this easier than his first-up effort, where he jumped a 40-1 chance in and Open 3YO race. Right back in grade now should help her chances and she has stacks of upside. Can run an improved race. ROCKY BEACH (4) will find this a lot easier than what she's been racing in, tackling Saturday grade for her first two starts. She's been out-paced over the short course and looks better suited to this race. Expecting a much better effort now. CASSANDRA (7) is a full sister to G1 placed Swiftfalcon and ticks a few boxes with Pike on board. Can feature. SLATERS LEGACY (6) won't be far away despite a disappointing debut effort.",
